1) The format: an era plays eight groups into a round of 16, the modern save keeps its shape
   34 careers played to the final whistle (34 era, 2 modern), 2 ended in the sack first
2) The draw: winners against runners-up, never the same group, never the same country, a function of the save
   33 draws checked, 264 ties, the association rule readable on 264 of them; every draw reproduced twice and across a save and reload
3) The group tables stay on the Cups tab once the knockouts start
   130 cards rendered through react-dom/server on knockout states
4) Level points split on head to head in Spain and Italy, on goal difference in England
   160 final tables read; 145 neighbouring pairs level on points in Spanish and Italian tables: 103 split on head to head points, 17 on head to head goal difference, 25 fell through to goal difference; 60 of them sit the other way round from goal difference (the visible change); 94 English level pairs, all on goal difference then goals scored
5) A pre migration save loads, is repaired honestly and plays out
   1 pre migration era save played to the final whistle with its round of 16; 7 wrong ledger shapes dropped; the modern save untouched
6) A Champions League group is sorted by the Champions League rule, and the round of 16 is seeded from that order
   1976 group tables read across 213 group nights, every one against the regulations' order rebuilt here from the ledger; 256 final groups checked against the round of 16 field; 8 crafted tables put through both group stage worlds and the modern save; 1 pre-478 save played its groups out with the results it lost left lost
   THE MEASUREMENT: of 272 groups at the final whistle, 91 finished with clubs level on points, the head to head put 29 of them in a different order from goal difference, and 12 of those changed who topped the group and therefore who hosts the deciding leg of the round of 16
7) An era European night names only men of that era, at every club of every era's field
   1512 era nights played across 4 eras (12 at each club of each field, plus the long names); 1411 opposition goals: 773 by men of the club's own era roster, 638 on the neutral shirt number line
   126 Match Centre previews of the same nights read, 134 danger men named, every one from the club's era roster
   49 of those goals were at the 5 clubs the pre-1028 draw handed today's scorers (era2005 Panathinaikos, era2010 Panathinaikos, era2015 Galatasaray, era2015 Paris Saint-Germain, era2015 Borussia Mönchengladbach); 13 at the Round 899 long names
